# LAN-first frontend environment template.
# Copy to frontend/.env.local once, then switch between LAN and ONLINE by
# commenting/uncommenting the blocks below. Update the LAN IPs when Wi-Fi changes.
# Both modes send REST requests through the same Next.js /backend proxy. The
# configured NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL selects the LAN or hosted backend upstream.
#
# ============================ LAN MODE =============================
NEXT_PUBLIC_EXAM_MODE=LAN
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://10.29.139.67:8080
NEXT_PUBLIC_AI_PROCTORING_URL=http://10.29.139.69:8000
NEXT_PUBLIC_AI_PROCTORING_WS_URL=ws://10.29.139.69:8000
ALLOWED_DEV_ORIGINS=10.29.139.74:3000
#
# ========================== ONLINE MODE ============================
# To use the hosted backend, comment the active LAN lines above and
# uncomment the ONLINE mode and endpoint lines below:
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_EXAM_MODE=ONLINE
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://quiz-app-production-24a8.up.railway.app
# NEXT_PUBLIC_AI_PROCTORING_URL=https://your-deployed-ai-service.example
# NEXT_PUBLIC_AI_PROCTORING_WS_URL=wss://your-deployed-ai-service.example
# ALLOWED_DEV_ORIGINS=localhost:3000
#
# NOTES:
# - NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL is the Spring Boot backend address.
# - ALLOWED_DEV_ORIGINS is a comma-separated list of host:port values for
#   the origins clients use to open Next.js in dev mode, without http:// or
#   https:// (for example, 10.29.139.74:3000).
# - Do not use 0.0.0.0 for ALLOWED_DEV_ORIGINS; it is only a bind address.
# - Keep only one active value for each variable.
# - AI proctoring uses NEXT_PUBLIC_AI_PROCTORING_URL (HTTP/HTTPS) and
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_AI_PROCTORING_WS_URL (WS/WSS). Configure them for the AI service
#   reachable from the browser; use localhost only when running it locally.
# - Restart Next.js after changing .env.local; rebuild for production.
